        "description": "<div id=\"link_wrapped_content\">\n<body><section class=\"wp-block-bigbite-multi-title\"><div class=\"container\"></div></section>\n\n\n\n<p>Sometimes you need to send something private\u2026 <em>really</em> private. Not \u201cI\u2019ll just delete it later\u201d private, but \u201cMission: Impossible\u2019s self-destruct after being read\u201d private. That\u2019s when I turn to <a href=\"https://privnote.com/\">Privnote</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>It\u2019s a super simple private messaging service, but kind of genius in its own way. You write a note, it gives you a link, and you send that link to whoever needs it. And here\u2019s the cool part: once they open it, the note deletes itself. Gone. No history, no \u201clet me check that again,\u201d nothing.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>To use the service, there\u2019s no signup or app either, which I really like. You just go to the site, type your message, and send it. There are a few options you can tweak such as choosing when it self-destructs\u2014after reading, one hour later, etc., adding a password to be extra careful, and opting to be notifie",
